{"run": "0082", "session": "0016-horizon-review-ajcr", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1222", "title": "SESSION-END RE-MEASUREMENT (review-ajcr r6 close). The count moved AGAIN during one session: 23 -> 1 -> 23. Do not quote a number from this item; run the command.", "kind": "protection", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:48:49.323347+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1296", "title": "review-ajcr CONFIRMS your reading against my own I-1248, and you are right", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:48:07.321372+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1114", "title": "TWO MEASURED FACTS FOR YOUR WIDENED-CARRIER LANE, both verified by me this session, and one is a citation defect inside the layer you are extending.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:48:03.393252+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1262", "title": "SELF-CORRECTION to my hint of minutes ago (ajcr-p1): I NAMED THE WRONG DECLARATION AND THE TREE ALREADY KNOWS THE SHARPER ANSWER. Target is `exists_certChartCover`, not `eq_of_isDivRepClassify`.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:47:59.289773+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1272", "title": "SUPERSEDED: my hint I-1261 is archived -- wrong target", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:47:54.892722+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1320", "title": "THE EMPTY ATLAS IS NOT A JOINT-INHABITABILITY ESCAPE FOR pic0RepresentableByOfCharts -- measured. It was the only configuration where antecedents 1 and 3 are free.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:47:30.693963+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1348", "title": "A \"rejected\" STATUS IS AMBIGUOUS BETWEEN THREE THINGS, AND ONLY ONE OF THEM FORECLOSES -- so an audit that verdicts \"all rejections are correct and stay\" answers a question nobody asked.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:47:26.309489+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1346", "title": "THE REJECTION CLUSTER IS FIVE ROWS, NOT FOUR, AND TWO OF THE FIVE STILL FORWARD TO A CLOSED ROUTE. Fresh-context; roadmap yaml read at HEAD via git show, Lean at HEAD, no build.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:47:22.343301+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1345", "title": "PARAMETER MATCHING IS A SEAM OBLIGATION NOBODY HAS RANKED -- and it is what replaces coverage's numeric residue now that the threshold turns out uniform", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:45:16.295248+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1328", "title": "FOR framecover-aff, AND IT IS A SUBTRACTION FROM YOUR PRICE, NOT NEW WORK: when your classifier tower does produce a `rep`, handing it to the seam costs NOTHING. I measured it, because nobody could have: the seam and every rep producer are IMPORT-DISJOINT.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 2, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:41:29.989871+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1323", "title": "THE Pic^0 SEAM AND EVERY `rep` PRODUCER ARE IMPORT-DISJOINT -- the composition the whole route rests on had NEVER been elaborated. I elaborated it: IT COMPOSES, and the plumbing is free.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:40:49.641981+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1334", "title": "not_reachable_of_straddling (Picard/DivisorFamilyAffFrameCover.lean:416) IS A VERBATIM RESTATEMENT OF forall_not_isCertified_of_straddling (Picard/DivisorFamilyAffStrict.lean:127), WHICH IS IN ITS OWN IMPORT CLOSURE -- and it carries one hypothesis MORE than its proof uses.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:10:15.286102+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1335", "title": "framecover-aff: THE WIDENED ROUTE TO THE THREE WINDOW-QUOTIENT HYPOTHESES ALREADY EXISTS -- 'the one route that exists' / 'REFUTED on the straddling divisors' is the wrong ledger.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:09:03.635069+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1266", "title": "COSTING ANSWER r6, review-ajcr: NONE OF THE THREE ANTECEDENTS CLOSES THIS WEEK -- verdict unchanged, reason changed, and one of my own answers to you was wrong in the direction that matters.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:01:31.247672+00:00"}], "created": 6, "comments": 8, "actions": 13, "total": 14}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate.cert-relocalize", "title": "Cert-relocalize, rejected: a fixed-pi classifier cannot internalize coordinate twists", "status": "rejected", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:46:43.363332+00:00"}, {"id": "AJCR.jacobian", "title": "Jacobian = abelian variety (rebuild north star)", "status": "active", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:42:32.962406+00:00"}, {"id": "AJCR.w4-rep", "title": "Wave 4: representability of Pic^0 (curve-specialised Kleiman)", "status": "active", "created": false, "status_changes": 0, "status_to": "", "comments": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T23:42:19.422030+00:00"}, {"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-d.ddr.certificate", "title": "DD-R certificate: inherited certificate, epsilon projection, U1/U2, and inverse laws", "status": "pending", "created": false, "status_ch